  "label": "Concentration camps",
  "description": "Concentration camps were camps established by Nazi Germany during World War II to imprison, torture, and murder millions of people, primarily Jews, but also other groups deemed undesirable by the regime. The image of prisoners in striped uniforms behind barbed wire is a direct reference to these camps, which are central to understanding the historical context of the image.",
